    "faqAccountTitle": "Access and account",
    "faqWhatIsQ": "What does Dermalyze do?",
    "faqWhatIsA": "Dermalyze supports the assessment of skin lesions. Triage classifies care priority from a photo, and Assisted Analysis, used by doctors, suggests a diagnostic hypothesis based on dermoscopy and clinical data. The final decision always belongs to the health professional.",
    "faqOfflineQ": "Does the app work offline?",
    "faqOfflineA": "Yes. Triage, Assisted Analysis and the Library work offline, because the analyses run on the device itself. Internet is only needed to sign in, create an account or reset your password.",
    "faqDataQ": "Is patient data saved?",
    "faqDataA": "No. Photos and clinical data stay on the device only during the analysis and are not sent to any server. The result is not kept: it is discarded when you start a new analysis or sign out.",
    "faqConfidenceQ": "What does model confidence mean?",
    "faqConfidenceA": "It is how sure the model is about the result, among the options it recognizes. It is not the chance that the lesion is malignant, nor a diagnostic confirmation. The lower the confidence, the more weight the clinical assessment should have.",
    "faqTriageHowQ": "How do I use Triage?",
    "faqTriageHowA": "In the Triage tab, tap the photo area, photograph the lesion without a dermatoscope and adjust the framing. If the photo is accepted, tap Analyze now. The result shows the priority level and the recommended management.",
    "faqPriorityLevelsQ": "What do levels P1 to P5 mean?",
    "faqPriorityLevelsA": "They are care priority levels, from the most urgent (P1, maximum priority) to the least urgent (P5, minimum priority). Each level is explained in the Library, under Methodology and Triage, and can also be opened on the result screen.",
    "faqPhotoRejectedQ": "Why was my photo rejected?",
    "faqPhotoRejectedA": "Before the analysis, the app checks whether the photo is sharp and shows a skin lesion. Blurry or dark photos, photos with glare or photos that do not show the skin are rejected. Follow the requirements shown on the capture screen and try again.",
    "faqDiagnosisHowQ": "How do I use Assisted Analysis?",
    "faqDiagnosisHowA": "In the Assisted Analysis tab, enter the age, skin cancer history, lesion region and symptoms. Then photograph the lesion with the attached dermatoscope. The result shows a diagnostic hypothesis, the priority level and the suggested management.",
    "faqReplacesDiagnosisQ": "Does the diagnostic hypothesis replace the doctor's diagnosis?",
    "faqReplacesDiagnosisA": "No. The hypothesis is decision support and does not replace the medical history, the clinical examination or the biopsy. Diagnosis and management are always the responsibility of the doctor.",
    "faqLibraryQ": "What is in the Library?",
    "faqLibraryA": "Reference material: the ABCDE rule for assessing pigmented lesions, the main skin diseases with search and filtering by characteristics, and the explanation of priority levels P1 to P5.",
    "faqPasswordQ": "I forgot my password. What do I do?",
    "faqPasswordA": "On the login screen, tap Forgot my password and enter your e-mail. You will receive a link to create a new password.",
    "faqAccessQ": "My access has not been granted. What do I do?",
    "faqAccessA": "Every registration must be approved by the Padtech team. Contact the team to request access; after that, just sign in again.",
    "faqLanguageQ": "How do I change the app language?",
    "faqLanguageA": "On the home screen, tap the gear icon and choose the language in Settings."
}
